WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.280
- I heard that you met
your girl on Instagram.

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:03.271
- I did, yeah.

00:00:03.271 --> 00:00:04.104
- That is crazy,

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.920
'cause that can go real
south, I'm just saying.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.460
- Well, here's what I did
though, here's what I did.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.293
- Okay.

00:00:08.293 --> 00:00:09.126
- 'Cause I knew it could go south

00:00:09.126 --> 00:00:11.010
because it's online dating, I mean--

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.254
- [Kelly] Yeah, and you're famous.

00:00:12.254 --> 00:00:13.313
- [Dustin] The position I was in,

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.146
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:14.979
it's tough to meet people.

00:00:14.979 --> 00:00:15.865
I don't get to go out a whole lot.

00:00:15.865 --> 00:00:16.698
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:16.698 --> 00:00:17.531
- [Dustin] So, I was like
you know what I'll do?

00:00:17.531 --> 00:00:19.820
I'll invite her to a
show and if she sucks,

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:20.940
I can just (Kelly laughing)

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.277
Or if its weird, I can just go,

00:00:22.277 --> 00:00:23.240
"Have fun at the show."

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.499
And security's there, gates
are there, I'm good Saint.

00:00:26.499 --> 00:00:27.520
- That's amazing!

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:28.940
- But see, she wasn't weird.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.339
- Oh, that's awesome!

00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:31.584
(audience clapping)

00:00:31.584 --> 00:00:32.802
- Always gotta have an out.

00:00:32.802 --> 00:00:35.917
- Have y'all ever met
someone on social media?

00:00:35.917 --> 00:00:37.630
You got married within
three months, Alano.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:38.549
- I did.

00:00:38.549 --> 00:00:39.850
That is a crazy great three months.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.816
- Yeah, and we've been
married for 11 years.

00:00:41.816 --> 00:00:42.649
- That's amazing.

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:44.788
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:44.788 --> 00:00:46.203
- I'm just saying if I'm
dating someone for three months

00:00:46.203 --> 00:00:48.257
and I'm like, "Wait getting married?

00:00:48.257 --> 00:00:49.490
"You haven't even seen the ugly side yet."

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:50.337
- That's what I said!

00:00:50.337 --> 00:00:53.177
She was like, "We'll figure
it out when we get married."

00:00:53.177 --> 00:00:54.500
- Did you guys get to do holidays

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.710
within those three months or is it--

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:56.543
- Nope.

00:00:56.543 --> 00:00:57.376
- No, wow.

00:00:57.376 --> 00:00:58.497
- No, I met her father
and you know he said,

00:00:58.497 --> 00:00:59.866
"Well if she'll have you, you can--"

00:00:59.866 --> 00:01:00.699
(everyone laughing)

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:02.459
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:02.459 --> 00:01:03.292
- I was like, "Okay."

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:04.912
- [Rosario] And they say romance is dead.

00:01:04.912 --> 00:01:07.129
- I know. I did the right thing.

00:01:07.129 --> 00:01:07.982
- [Kelly] You did.

00:01:07.982 --> 00:01:08.815
- I'm from the south, so I
went to talk to her father

00:01:08.815 --> 00:01:10.290
and he said, "Well, she'll have you."

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.983
So okay. That's I blessing I guess.

00:01:14.286 --> 00:01:15.193
- I guess you're fine.

00:01:15.193 --> 00:01:17.050
(Kelly and Alano laughing)

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.290
Also, this is hilarious.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.029
I hear you have--it's not
hilarious it's awesome

00:01:20.029 --> 00:01:22.390
I have a girl crush on her as well but--

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:23.684
- [Kelly] You love Reba McEntire.

00:01:23.684 --> 00:01:24.550
- Oh, yes.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:25.581
- That is amazing!

00:01:25.581 --> 00:01:27.508
- She's always been my celebrity crush.

00:01:27.508 --> 00:01:28.682
(audience cheering)

00:01:28.682 --> 00:01:29.941
- [Kelly] Yes! Look at you!

00:01:29.941 --> 00:01:31.066
- [Dustin] There we are!

00:01:31.066 --> 00:01:32.329
- [Kelly] That's so great!

00:01:32.329 --> 00:01:35.360
- That's one of the
coolest nights of my life.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.160
That's me getting inducted
into the Grand Ole Opry family.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.094
- That is so amazing.

00:01:39.094 --> 00:01:40.460
- I can't believe that was a surprise.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:43.237
- With Reba there. That's amazing!

00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:45.680
- I told my team I don't wanna
know who's gonna come out

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.060
and do the official induction
- [Kelly] Oh, yeah.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.990
- And freaking Reba McEntire walked out.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:53.140
- Oh my gosh. And she's
so nice, she's so lovely.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.020
- I have a weird object in my basement

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.760
that all my friends that come over

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:57.593
who haven't been there yet--

00:01:57.593 --> 00:01:59.466
- I'm so excited by what's
about to come out of your mouth.

00:01:59.466 --> 00:02:00.660
(laughing)

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.960
- You have a weird object
in your basement, go.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.470
- Yeah so, I did a trophy
case from that night

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:06.917
with Reba, from the Grand Ole Opry

00:02:06.917 --> 00:02:09.240
and it's that trophy

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.000
and then there's this
tissue paper that's there

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.180
and people are like, "What is that?"

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.460
And so we started crying,

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.070
she was saying such sweet
and important things to me

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.340
I started bawling on stage.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.227
And then she goes, "And
to sing his first song

00:02:21.227 --> 00:02:23.160
"as the Grand Ole Opry
member, here's Dustin Lynch."

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.190
And I'm just a mess, crying on stage.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:26.697
And she ran offstage, grabs me tissues,

00:02:26.697 --> 00:02:28.950
and then runs back onstage
and hands me tissues.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.810
So, that's my weird object. That tissue--

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:31.643
- Oh my god!

00:02:31.643 --> 00:02:33.858
- [Dustin] That is weird
right? It's kinda gross.

00:02:33.858 --> 00:02:35.609
- That's not weird! That's really sweet.

00:02:35.609 --> 00:02:40.290
You made yourself sound like
some kind of serial killer,

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.140
and now you're actually really sweet.

00:02:43.458 --> 00:02:45.010
- It is kinda creepy
though, I save tissues--

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.350
- It's not creepy! It's not creepy.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.760
If Meryl Streep handed me something

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.540
she was crying on, I'd keep it.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:51.373
- There in a frame?

00:02:51.373 --> 00:02:54.200
- (Kelly laughing) Oh,
yeah, yes, with a plaque.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.251
She touched my face!

00:02:55.251 --> 00:02:58.110
I'm just kidding, Meryl.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.660
You planned on studying medicine,

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.517
which I think is amazing.

00:03:01.517 --> 00:03:03.470
You got accepted into a
school, you were gonna go--

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.303
- As a surgeon, yeah.

00:03:04.303 --> 00:03:06.850
- How did parents take that news?

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:07.710
- Not great.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:08.543
- [Kelly] Yeah, I don't think so.

00:03:08.543 --> 00:03:09.503
- Not at all no.

00:03:09.503 --> 00:03:11.185
I mean, I promised my
parents I would graduate

00:03:11.185 --> 00:03:13.440
and when I got to college, I fell in love

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.490
with how the human body works,

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.966
so it's a natural progression
to get to med school.

00:03:16.966 --> 00:03:19.070
But then, I just had this,
"What if?" down inside

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.707
and I was like, "Man I
gotta chase this dream.

00:03:21.707 --> 00:03:22.865
"I have to try it."
- Yeah.

00:03:22.865 --> 00:03:24.550
- If it doesn't work out, fine.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.530
But I went and told my
parents that I would be

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.400
putting off med school to go and play

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.497
for tips in a jar at a hockey time.

00:03:30.497 --> 00:03:31.422
Trying to make rent--

00:03:31.422 --> 00:03:32.940
- Oh my god. That's every parents' dream.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:33.860
- My dad backed me up

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:35.510
to the wall in the hallway pretty quick.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:38.523
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's a southern daddy.

00:03:40.071 --> 00:03:40.904
- But it worked out.

00:03:40.904 --> 00:03:41.800
- So here is the best part, though.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.798
So I hear that the only C you've received

00:03:43.798 --> 00:03:45.896
in high school was in music class.

00:03:45.896 --> 00:03:47.512
- Yes. That's it.

00:03:47.512 --> 00:03:49.457
And more importantly, vocal music.

00:03:49.457 --> 00:03:50.723
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:50.723 --> 00:03:51.830
Vocal music too, is the class.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.769
- So after your parents knowing that,

00:03:53.769 --> 00:03:56.420
did it make harder?

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.055
- That's probably what
they were leaning on.

00:03:58.055 --> 00:04:00.310
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.310
- But honestly, at that point,

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:03.340
I had been playing at a lot
of bars and frat parties,

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.140
a lot of college events
around the south east.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:05.973
- Yeah.

00:04:05.973 --> 00:04:08.334
- So, I think they were a
little bit confused, you know?

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:09.170
- Yeah.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.751
- So, they gave me their blessing and--

00:04:10.751 --> 00:04:11.890
- Yeah, you gotta follow your dream.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:12.723
You want your baby to follow their dreams.

00:04:12.723 --> 00:04:14.720
- And honestly, dad, I thought he was

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.044
gonna punch me in my
throat whenever I told him.

00:04:17.044 --> 00:04:17.877
- Yup, southern dad.

00:04:17.877 --> 00:04:21.810
- But he was the first guy to
be driving us to and from gigs

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.411
and helping us set up
right after that, so.

00:04:23.411 --> 00:04:25.510
- That's so cool!

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.909
They've gotten to do this
whole thing with you.

00:04:26.909 --> 00:04:27.742
- I know, yeah--

00:04:27.742 --> 00:04:30.339
- And then you're with
Reba McIntire onstage

00:04:30.339 --> 00:04:32.860
doing your tears with your tissues.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.563
Show the tissue all the
time to your family.

00:04:34.563 --> 00:04:35.800
(Dustin laughing)

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.230
So we've been asking everybody

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:38.790
what their campaign slogan would be,

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.009
your presidential campaign slogan.

00:04:40.009 --> 00:04:40.842
- Yes.

00:04:40.842 --> 00:04:43.360
- So it's your name, it's
the year you wanna run,

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.969
and it's your last text.

00:04:44.969 --> 00:04:47.219
- Okay.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:48.270
I know what it is, actually.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:51.400
Dustin Lynch, 2048, drink, drink, drink.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.483
(everyone cheering)

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.551
- Oh god!

00:04:56.551 --> 00:04:57.384
- [Dustin] That would work.

00:04:57.384 --> 00:04:59.880
- [Kelly] I mean, y'all's
totally beats mine.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.320
Mine was so dumb.
- [Dustin] What was yours?

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.850
- I'm so mad, I'm so
competitive. Mine is so long

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:04.720
I don't even remember
it; I was apologizing

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.099
'cause I didn't return some text

00:05:06.099 --> 00:05:07.888
and I was so long-winded about it.

00:05:07.888 --> 00:05:09.866
(gasps) I'm dumb.

00:05:09.866 --> 00:05:10.765
- Grimace face was great though.

00:05:10.765 --> 00:05:12.257
I send grimace faces all the time.

00:05:12.257 --> 00:05:13.610
- [Kelly] Yeah grimace
face is the last one.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:14.456
- Grimace face.

00:05:14.456 --> 00:05:15.289
(Dustin laughing)

